      },
      {
        "name": "explanation",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "It clearly sets the fixed per-job cost against the test time and notes that every shard re-paid the install, but it draws the figures from one run, omits the count-based 8/8/8 split, the 36s third-shard stagger and the noise between the two shard samples, and overstates the install saving ('most of the 48s') when much of it is apt dependencies Chromium still needs, though it does label the 45-55s figure as an unmeasured estimate."
      }
    ],
